---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { COMPANY } from '../consts';

const LAST_UPDATED = '2026-09-22';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How this site handles personal data: hosting, cookieless analytics, and the contact form."
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-neutral-600">
    Last updated: <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{LAST_UPDATED}</time>
  </p>

  <p class="mt-8 leading-relaxed">
    This policy describes what this website actually does with personal data. It is short
    because the site does very little: it serves static pages, counts page views without
    cookies, and forwards contact form messages by email.
  </p>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Controller</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      {COMPANY.legalName}, {COMPANY.street}, {COMPANY.postalCode} {COMPANY.city}, {
        COMPANY.country
      }. Registry code {COMPANY.regNo}. Managing director {COMPANY.director}.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      For data protection questions, including any request listed in section 7, write to <a
        href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}
        class="underline hover:no-underline">{COMPANY.email}</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. Hosting</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. To deliver pages and to protect the site
      against attacks, Cloudflare processes your IP address and request metadata such as the
      time of the request, the page requested, the referrer, and your browser's user agent.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Legal basis: legitimate interest in operating a secure and available website,
      Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Cloudflare acts as a processor on behalf of the controller.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Analytics</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      The site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics. It is cookieless: it sets no cookies, does not
      fingerprint your device or browser, and does not track you across other sites. It
      collects only aggregated page-view data, such as how often a page was viewed and the
      broad referrer category.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Legal basis: legitimate interest in understanding which pages are read,
      Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      This is why the site shows no cookie banner. A consent banner is required for storing
      or reading information on your device that is not strictly necessary. Nothing here
      stores or reads anything, so there is nothing to consent to.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      This site sets no cookies and uses no local storage, session storage, or comparable
      technology.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Contact form</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      The contact form on the homepage collects your name, your email address, and your
      message. These are used to read and answer your enquiry, and for nothing else.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where the enquiry concerns a contract or steps taken
      before entering one, and otherwise legitimate interest in answering messages sent to
      the company, Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Submissions are delivered by email through Resend (Resend, Inc., United States), which
      acts as a processor. The transfer to the United States relies on the EU-US Data
      Privacy Framework and on standard contractual clauses.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      The form contains a hidden spam-prevention field, a honeypot. It is invisible to
      people and to screen readers, so it collects nothing from real visitors; only
      automated submissions fill it in, and those are discarded.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Retention: enquiries are kept only as long as needed to handle them and any follow-up,
      then deleted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">6. RSS feed</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      The feed at <a href="/rss.xml" class="underline hover:no-underline">/rss.xml</a> is a
      static file. Requesting it collects nothing beyond the hosting data described in
      section 2.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">7. Your rights</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      You have the right to access your personal data, to have it corrected or erased, to
      restrict its processing, to receive it in a portable form, and to object to processing
      based on legitimate interest.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. The
      competent authority here is the Estonian Data Protection Inspectorate (Andmekaitse
      Inspektsioon), <a href="https://www.aki.ee/en" class="underline hover:no-underline"
        >https://www.aki.ee/en</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">8. What this site does not do</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      There is no profiling and no automated decision-making. Personal data is not sold, and
      it is not shared with advertising networks. The site carries no advertising, no social
      media embeds, and no third-party trackers beyond the hosting and analytics described
      above.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
